---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { route } from '../i18n/routes';
const lang = 'en';
---
<PageLayout title="Cookies on Tax Invoice Maker: none, and what your browser keeps" description="No cookies on this invoice generator. What it keeps in your browser's local storage for the next invoice, how to delete it, and the cookie-free stability monitoring." lang={lang} noindex={true} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Cookies' }]} showAuthor={false}>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <h1>Cookies</h1>
    <p>No page of the site sets a cookie, advertising or otherwise.</p>
    <h2>What stays in your browser</h2>
    <p>So that you do not retype them, the generator keeps your own business details in your browser's local storage on this device: business name, address, email, tax number, logo, payment details, notes, country and last invoice number. This is not a cookie and it is never sent to us. The "Forget my details" link under the generator's checklist deletes it, and so does clearing the site data in your browser. Customer details and invoice lines are not kept.</p>
    <h2>Anonymous stability monitoring</h2>
    <p>To find broken pages, script errors and slow loading, the site can load Microsoft Clarity, from Microsoft Ireland Operations Limited, in its cookie-free mode. Clarity then sets no cookie, gives each page view a one-off identifier and does not link visits. Everything typed in the generator, and the invoice preview, is masked before anything is sent. Blocking the clarity.ms domain stops this monitoring without affecting the generator.</p>
    <p>The <a href={route('privacy', lang)}>privacy policy</a> explains who receives the monitoring data and for how long.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
